Third-party libraries in the release packages (not in this repository):

- FFmpeg 9.0.2 libavcodec + libavutil, LGPL-2.1-or-later, linked statically
  into the Linux and macOS releases for the phone mirror's and AirPlay's video
  and AirPlay's audio. Built with the H.264, AAC and ALAC decoders only (no GPL
  parts, no external codec libraries) by
  packaging/ffmpeg/build-h264-decoder.sh from the signed release tarball
  https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz; that script holds the exact
  configure flags. To relink OCTAVE against another FFmpeg, build from this
  repository with -DOCTAVE_FFMPEG_ROOT=<prefix> or without it (system FFmpeg).
  The Windows release ships vcpkg's ffmpeg[core,avcodec] DLLs (LGPL-2.1-or-later).
- Qt 6 (LGPL-3.0; GPL-3.0 for Qt Quick 3D and Qt Quick Timeline), linked
  dynamically. Qt Multimedia's FFmpeg backend carries its own FFmpeg, which
  Qt builds LGPL, except in the Linux aarch64 AppImage: there the Qt package
  links Ubuntu 22.04's FFmpeg 4.4 (libavcodec58 and friends, GPL-2.0-or-later
  with x264 / x265 / xvid), and the AppImage bundles those libraries. Their
  source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/ffmpeg (jammy-updates) and the
  x264, x265 and xvidcore source packages of the same release.
- TagLib (LGPL-2.1 / MPL-1.1), linked dynamically, desktop only.
- libplist 2.x (LGPL-2.1-or-later), linked dynamically, Linux only (AirPlay).
- Android platform-tools (adb), Apache-2.0, shipped next to the binary.
